{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"agent_message","text":"The first scoring pass is deliberately conservative: it produced zero false positives, but recall is still short. Two mechanical issues account for many misses (slash-form vessel prefixes and one-word weak aliases). I also found one over-broad equivalence introduced by learning alias spellings transitively, so I’m tracing that before raising recall; the goal is to keep the current decoy performance intact."}}
